  "tagline": "AWS's MPP columnar data warehouse, available as provisioned RA3 clusters or Serverless.",
  "description": "Amazon Redshift is AWS's managed data warehouse, descended from ParAccel and speaking the PostgreSQL wire protocol. RA3 nodes keep hot data on local SSD and the rest in Redshift Managed Storage on S3, and Redshift Serverless removes node sizing entirely. It integrates deeply with the AWS estate: zero-ETL from Aurora and DynamoDB, Spectrum queries over S3, streaming ingestion from Kinesis and MSK, and data sharing between clusters. It is the natural default for AWS-centric shops, though it still asks for more tuning (sort keys, workload management) than Snowflake or BigQuery.",
